<title>INDIA: India's Nagarjuna Fert 1996/97 net falls.</title>
<headline>India's Nagarjuna Fert 1996/97 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    1,552.4 vs  2,211.8</p>
<p>    Income		  9,224.9 vs  8,822.7</p>
<p>    Other income	    274.1 vs    458.4</p>
<p>    Expenditure	   5,456.5 vs  5,117.8</p>
<p>    Interest		1,425.4 vs  1,235.0</p>
<p>    Gross profit	  2,617.1 vs  2,928.3</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    766.1 vs    716.5</p>
<p>    Tax			 298.6 vs    Nil</p>
<p>Note: Nagarjuna Fertilisers, based in Hyderabad, is an Indian fertiliser manufacturer. The firm said in a statement that the results were audited and had been taken on record at a meeting of the board on April 24. A dividend of 18 percent has been declared for the financial year ending March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
